<configs>

	<!--
		=========================================================================
		PROJECT PRAXIS - THE PACK'S FRONT PAGE
		=========================================================================

		This modlet exists to describe the pack and nothing else. It ships no blocks, no
		items, no recipes and no code - only the text that appears on the main menu Mod
		Summary panel, plus the one line that switches that panel on.

		[ WHY IT IS ITS OWN MODLET ]
		The description used to live in SphereII A Round World, which was wrong: that is a
		standalone quality of life modlet that people install on its own, and it has no
		business claiming to speak for a ten modlet overhaul it happens to ship inside.
		Pack level text belongs to the pack.

		Keeping it separate also means the wording can be changed without touching, or
		re-releasing, any modlet that actually does something.

		[ THE NAME ]
		"ZZ-" so it sorts last. Mods apply in alphabetical order of folder name, and a
		modlet patching a window that does not exist yet is skipped in full and silently,
		so anything contributing to the panel has to load after 0-Help Screens declares
		it. Sorting last also means this modlet gets the final word if any other file
		touches the same tabs.

		[ WHAT IT OWNS ]
		Registering the panel (see this modlet's XUi_Menu/xui.xml - that append into the
		mainMenu window_group is what makes it appear at all), and all four of its tabs.

		The strip holds four and About is one of them, so this file repoints About at the
		pack overview and spends the other three. THE PANEL IS FULL - a fifth page would
		hand XUiC_TabSelectorTab.TabSelected a null TabButton, since it indexes Tabs[i]
		against tabButtons[i] with no guard. Going further needs both of these first:

		    <set xpath="/windows/window[@name='mainMenuHelpScreens']//grid[@name='tabButtons']/@cols">5</set>
		    <set xpath="/windows/window[@name='mainMenuHelpScreens']//grid[@name='tabButtons']/@cell_width">86</set>

		and captions shrink to fit their cell, so five is about the limit at 450px wide.

		[ THE PACK IT DESCRIBES ]
		    0-SCore, 0_TFP_Harmony      framework
		    0-Help Screens              this panel and the in-game help screen
		    SphereII Learn By Doing     use-based progression
		    SphereII A Round World      quality of life, the Drop Box
		    SphereII Challenges         80 extra challenges
		    SphereII Peace of Mind      softened imagery and language
		    SphereII Disable Sway       no camera or weapon sway
		    SphereII Disable Special..  Chuck and the Rancher melee only
		    Locks                       lock picking minigame
		    ZZTong-Prefabs              233 POIs, 128 decorations, 58 RWG tiles
		    ZZ-ModInfo                  this - the pack's name and description

		Keep that list and the text in step when the pack changes. The ZZTong counts came
		from the .tts files under its Prefabs folder rather than from its README, which
		gives no totals; the text rounds them rather than quoting them, so a version bump
		does not immediately make it wrong.

		THE ZZTONG ATTRIBUTION IS NOT DECORATION - DO NOT TRIM IT. That modlet is GPLv3
		and its README asks that anyone bundling the POIs credit the author, naming the
		handle "ZZTong" or "zztong" specifically. The Comfort page therefore names both
		the modlet (ZZTong Prefabs) and the author (ZZTong) in as many words. It is the
		only third party content in this pack and the only entry carrying that obligation.

		Two more player facing details from that README are worth keeping in the Comfort
		page if it is ever rewritten: some of the hunters' traps are lethal, and the pack
		has to be on the server AND every client, because server side alone loses POI
		names and some trigger wiring.

		[ ONE MORE HONEST NOTE, ON THE CHALLENGES PAGE ]
		SphereII Challenges ships eight NPC hiring challenges, and this pack installs no
		NPC modlet - there is no entity_class starting with "npc" anywhere in it. That
		category is visible and can never be completed here, so the page says so rather
		than leaving players hunting for something that is not there.

		Wrapped in a conditional because the target window only exists if 0-Help Screens
		is installed. mod_loaded() takes the ModInfo.xml <Name value="..."/>.
	-->
	<conditional>
		<if cond="mod_loaded('sphereii_help_screens')">

			<!--
				The panel is switched on in this modlet's XUi_Menu/xui.xml, by appending
				the window into the mainMenu window_group. It is not done here, and it is
				not a visibility attribute - XUiV_Window.OnOpen forces IsVisible true
				whenever its group opens, so an XML flag never survives. This file only
				supplies content.
			-->

			<!--
				Replace the placeholder About body with the pack overview. Tab 0 is what
				opens, so that is where the general description belongs. The tab keeps its
				"About" caption, which is the right word for it - only the body moves.

				This patches a template INSTANTIATION, not a template's internals. The
				helpmenu_page element is an ordinary node with ordinary attributes right up
				until templates expand, and XPath patching runs before that - the same
				timing that makes it impossible to append INTO a template.
			-->
			<set xpath="/windows/window[@name='mainMenuHelpScreens']//helpmenu_page[@tab_key='helpMenuAbout']/@text_key">zzPackOverviewBody</set>

			<append xpath="/windows/window[@name='mainMenuHelpScreens']//rect[@name='tabsContents']">

				<helpmenu_page tab_key="zzPackProgression" text_key="zzPackProgressionBody" />
				<helpmenu_page tab_key="zzPackComfort"     text_key="zzPackComfortBody" />
				<helpmenu_page tab_key="zzPackChallenges"  text_key="zzPackChallengesBody" />

			</append>

		</if>
	</conditional>

</configs>